  "properties": {
    "title": "China Dimensions Data Collection: Priority Programme for China's Agenda 21",
    "description": "The Priority Programme for China's Agenda 21 consists of full-text program descriptions supporting China's economic and social development. The descriptions represent 69 programs covering legislation, policy, education, agriculture, environment, energy, transportation, regional development, population, health, and global change research. Each description includes project scope, background, objectives, activities, inputs, and benefits. This data set is produced in collaboration with the Administrative Center for China's Agenda 21 (ACCA21), United Nations Development Programme (UNDP), and the Columbia University Center for International Earth Science Information Network (CIESIN).",
    "license": "None | The Administrative Center for China's Agenda 21 (ACCA21), United Nations Development Programme (UNDP), and Trustees of Columbia University in the City of New York hold the copyright of this data set. Users are prohibited from any commercial, non-free resale, or redistribution without explicit written permission from ACCA21, UNDP, and CIESIN. Users should acknowledge ACCA21, UNDP, and CIESIN as the source used in the creation of any reports, publications, new data sets, derived products, or services resulting from the use of this data set. ACCA21, UNDP, and CIESIN also request reprints of any publications and notification of any redistributing efforts.",
